@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Order & Crafting Process — SAT Jewel";
}

<div class="op-page-wrap">
    <!-- Header Section -->
    <div class="op-header-section">
        <div class="op-breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> &rsaquo; <span>Order Process</span></div>
        <h1 class="op-main-title">Order Process</h1>
        <p class="op-subtitle">Unsure about what occurs once you've placed an order? This educational page about the order cycle/process will provide guidance on the Sat Jewels ordering procedure.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Main Content Section (Verbatim copy from media_1787461024047.md) -->
    <div class="op-container">
        <div class="op-explanation-box">
            <h2 class="op-section-title">What occurs after placing an order with Sat Jewels?</h2>
            <p class="op-lead-text">At Sat Jewels, all our fine jewelry pieces are exclusively Made-to-Order. Since every design is tailored specifically for you, our dedicated crafting phase takes approximately 8 to 10 business days before dispatch. Here is a step-by-step overview of what happens after you place an order with Sat Jewels:</p>

            <div class="op-step-block">
                <ul class="op-substep-list" style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 12px;"><strong>3D CAD Modeling:</strong> We create a precise 3D Computer-Aided Design (CAD) based on your chosen ring size, gemstone specifications, and metal selection.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 12px;"><strong>Wax Printing &amp; Metal Casting:</strong> The finalized 3D design is converted into a high-precision wax pattern, followed by the molten metal casting process.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 12px;"><strong>Pre-Polishing &amp; Metal Prep:</strong> The raw casted piece undergoes initial smoothing and pre-polishing to prepare the metal beds for stone placement.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 12px;"><strong>Master Diamond Setting:</strong> Expert artisans delicately handset each diamond, carefully aligning and adjusting the prongs to secure every stone perfectly.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 12px;"><strong>Final Mirror Polish &amp; Finishing:</strong> The ring undergoes a final multi-stage polishing and plating process to give it a brilliant, high-grade luster.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 12px;"><strong>Strict Quality Inspection:</strong> A senior quality manager inspects the finished piece to ensure structural integrity and check for any manufacturing defects.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 12px;"><strong>Final Client Photo Approval:</strong> Before shipping, we share high-resolution photos and videos of your finished jewelry piece for your review and satisfaction.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- 4-Step Timeline Confirmation Grid (Verbatim copy from media_1787461024047.md) -->
    <div class="op-timeline-section">
        <div class="op-timeline-container">
            <div class="op-timeline-grid">
                <!-- Step 1 -->
                <div class="op-card">
                    <div class="op-card-icon">
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-cube"></i>
                    </div>
                    <h3 class="op-card-title">1. 3D CAD Preview &amp; Digital Approval</h3>
                    <p class="op-card-desc">Once your order is successfully placed with Sat Jewels, our design team creates an intricate 3D Computer-Aided Design (CAD) model of your jewelry piece. This digital rendering provides a realistic 3D representation, allowing you to preview the exact dimensions, prong placements, and overall aesthetic before actual physical crafting begins. We share these detailed CAD images with you for review to ensure every specification meets your complete satisfaction.</p>
                </div>

                <!-- Step 2 -->
                <div class="op-card">
                    <div class="op-card-icon">
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-gem"></i>
                    </div>
                    <h3 class="op-card-title">2. Diamond Verification &amp; Inspection</h3>
                    <p class="op-card-desc">Following CAD design approval, Sat Jewels provides high-resolution photographs and studio videos of the selected diamonds for your personal review. This step allows you to inspect the stone's clarity, cut, color, and brilliance up close, ensuring complete confidence in the diamond selected for your custom piece before it is handset into the mounting.</p>
                </div>

                <!-- Step 3 -->
                <div class="op-card">
                    <div class="op-card-icon">
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-ring"></i>
                    </div>
                    <h3 class="op-card-title">3. Artisanal Crafting &amp; Manufacturing</h3>
                    <p class="op-card-desc">Upon receiving your approval on both the CAD blueprint and the loose diamond, Sat Jewels initiates the handcrafting phase. Our master jewelers utilize time-honored techniques and modern precision to cast, assemble, and detail your piece. We ensure superior structural integrity and an exceptional level of mirror-like finishing throughout every stage of creation.</p>
                </div>

                <!-- Step 4 -->
                <div class="op-card">
                    <div class="op-card-icon">
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-wand-magic-sparkles"></i>
                    </div>
                    <h3 class="op-card-title">4. Finished Piece Inspection &amp; Shipping Authorization</h3>
                    <p class="op-card-desc">As soon as your custom jewelry piece is fully crafted and polished, Sat Jewels captures high-definition media (photographs and showcase videos) of the complete item. We send these visuals to you for a final review. Once you inspect the finished product and give us your explicit approval, we securely package and dispatch your order.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Have Any Questions Section (From media_1787461024047.md) -->
    <div style="max-width: 1000px; margin: 60px auto 40px; padding: 0 24px;">
        <h2 style="font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif; font-size: 2.2rem; font-weight: 700; text-align: center; color: #ffffff; margin-bottom: 32px;">Have Any Questions?</h2>

        <div style="background: #0b1524; color: #ffffff; border-radius: 12px; padding: 24px; margin-bottom: 20px; box-shadow: 0 4px 14px rgba(0,0,0,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(212, 178, 112, 0.25);">
            <h3 style="font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 700; color: #ffffff; margin: 0 0 10px;">Will I be able to preview and approve the diamond before my jewelry is crafted?</h3>
            <p style="color: #cbd5e1; font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0;">
                Yes, completely! At Sat Jewels, we strictly prioritize client confidence and total transparency. Prior to setting the gemstone into your piece, our team shares detailed high-definition photography and studio video footage of the selected loose diamond. This allows you to closely inspect its cut, brilliance, and overall quality, ensuring that the stone fully aligns with your standards before production moves forward.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div style="background: #0b1524; color: #ffffff; border-radius: 12px; padding: 24px; margin-bottom: 20px; box-shadow: 0 4px 14px rgba(0,0,0,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(212, 178, 112, 0.25);">
            <h3 style="font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 700; color: #ffffff; margin: 0 0 10px;">Do you share 3D CAD blueprints for order approval?</h3>
            <p style="color: #cbd5e1; font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0;">
                Yes, absolutely. Every bespoke order at Sat Jewels includes a dedicated 3D CAD model rendering step. We share these high-resolution digital blueprints with you prior to metal casting so you can inspect prong layouts, band widths, and stone elevations from all angles.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

